                    <p className="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-6 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
                      {item.text}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </section>

        {/* =================================================
            DESIGN DECISIONS
        ================================================= */}

        <section className="border-t border-black/[0.08] px-5 py-24 dark:border-white/[0.08] sm:px-8 sm:py-28 lg:px-14">
          <Reveal>
            <SectionNumber number="07" label="Design decisions" />

            <div className="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.5fr] lg:gap-12">
              <h2 className="font-serif text-[38px] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-[52px]">
                Less friction, not more features.
              </h2>

              <div className="space-y-6 text-[16px] leading-7 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 sm:text-[18px] sm:leading-8">
                <div>
                  <h3 className="font-medium text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
                    Clear hierarchy
                  </h3>

                  <p className="mt-2">
                    Important information is visually prioritized so
                    users can scan before they decide.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <h3 className="font-medium text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
                    Consistent patterns
                  </h3>

                  <p className="mt-2">
                    Similar actions and states behave consistently
                    across the experience.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <h3 className="font-medium text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
                    Action-oriented interfaces
                  </h3>

                  <p className="mt-2">
                    Each screen is designed to make the next useful
                    action easier to understand.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </section>

        {/* =================================================
            TRADE OFFS
        ================================================= */}

        <section className="border-t border-black/[0.08] px-5 py-24 dark:border-white/[0.08] sm:px-8 sm:py-28 lg:px-14">
          <Reveal>
            <SectionNumber number="08" label="Trade-offs" />

            <div className="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.5fr] lg:gap-12">
              <h2 className="font-serif text-[38px] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-[52px]">
                Keep the product useful without making it feel heavy.
              </h2>

              <div className="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-7 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 sm:text-[18px] sm:leading-8">
                <p>
                  Recruitment platforms can contain a large amount
                  of information. Adding everything to the primary
                  experience would make it harder to scan.
                </p>

                <p>
                  I therefore focused the primary screens on the
                  information required for the current decision and
                  kept secondary information available when needed.
                </p>

                <p>
                  This helped maintain a balance between a rich
                  product experience and a manageable interface.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </section>

        {/* =================================================
            ROLE
        ================================================= */}

        <section className="border-t border-black/[0.08] px-5 py-24 dark:border-white/[0.08] sm:px-8 sm:py-28 lg:px-14">
          <Reveal>
            <SectionNumber number="09" label="My role" />

            <div className="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.5fr] lg:gap-12">
              <h2 className="font-serif text-[38px] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-[52px]">
                Designing the experience from structure to interface.
              </h2>

              <div className="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-7 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 sm:text-[18px] sm:leading-8">
                <p>
                  I was responsible for the UX/UI design of the
                  experience, including information architecture,
                  user flows, interface structure and high-fidelity
                  UI design.
                </p>

                <p>
                  I worked through the relationship between
                  different parts of the recruitment journey and
                  translated those requirements into a consistent
                  product experience.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </section>

        {/* =================================================
            LEARNING
        ================================================= */}

        <section className="border-t border-black/[0.08] px-5 py-28 dark:border-white/[0.08] sm:px-8 sm:py-32 lg:px-14">
          <Reveal>
            <SectionNumber number="10" label="What I learned" />

            <div className="mt-10 max-w-[1000px]">
              <blockquote className="font-serif text-[36px] leading-[1.12] tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-[54px]">
                “Good product design doesn't just organize
                information. It helps people make decisions.”
              </blockquote>

              <p className="mt-8 max-w-[720px] text-[16px] leading-7 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 sm:mt-10 sm:text-[18px] sm:leading-8">
                This project reinforced the importance of designing
                around the user's next action rather than treating
                each screen as an isolated interface. When the
                structure is clear, the UI becomes much easier to
                understand.
              </p>
            </div>
          </Reveal>
        </section>

        {/* =================================================
